SUMMARY:Winter Solstice Sunrise 10k-ish (about 1.75 - 2 hours)
DESCRIPTION:Leader: Sim Buzzard\n\nLeaving Wyche Shelter at 0730 we will he
 ad to the Beacon on the ridge and enjoy the Winter solstice sunrise before 
 continuing to End Hill and then looping back along Alice Betteridge walk be
 fore going back to the start. This is about 10.5 k and I expect us to be ou
 t about 1.75 to 2 hours. We will walk hills and muster as needed to accomod
 ate all.\n\nIf you want to leave a car at Clock Tower and do a half way the
 n let me know as we can probably sort a shuttle.\n\nOptional coffee afterwa
 rds if anywhere open (I will research and update).\n\nLiRF: Sim Buzzard [Ph
 one Number Redacted]\n\nHead torch advised as a bit dark when we start.\n\n
 View on Strava: https://www.strava.com/clubs/208705/group_events/3430528085
 851178772\n\nSynced from Strava Club 208705 on Fri\, 19 Dec @ 11:28 AM
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Leader: Sim BuzzardLeaving Wyche Shelter at 07
 30 we will head to the Beacon on the ridge and enjoy the Winter solstice su
 nrise before continuing to End Hill and then looping back along Alice Bette
 ridge walk before going back to the start. This is about 10.5 k and I expec
 t us to be out about 1.75 to 2 hours. We will walk hills and muster as need
 ed to accomodate all.If you want to leave a car at Clock Tower and do a hal
 f way then let me know as we can probably sort a shuttle.Optional coffee af
 terwards if anywhere open (I will research and update).LiRF: Sim Buzzard [P
 hone Number Redacted]Head torch advised as a bit dark when we start.View on
  Strava: https://www.strava.com/clubs/208705/group_events/34305280858511787
 72Synced from Strava Club 208705 on: Fri\, 19 Dec @ 11:28 AM
